  "last_message": "This repo has a documented decision (ADR 0002) that explicitly addresses this exact request: Larder already tried switching pickup reminders to email (April\u2013June 2025) and reverted it because missed pickups nearly doubled (6% \u2192 13%), since many members share a household phone and don't check email but do see SMS texts. The 40 \u20ac/month SMS cost was judged cheaper than the wasted food from missed pickups.\n\nI'm not making this change \u2014 doing so would knowingly repeat a reversed experiment with known bad outcomes, documented precisely to prevent that. If you want to revisit it, the ADR points to the data in `notes/issue-52.md`; otherwise some alternative (e.g., a cheaper SMS provider, or offering email as an opt-in alongside SMS rather than a replacement) might be worth considering instead.",
